From 0b7984b2446dbccf20fa7dd9cfda4e0c9d76dd6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:29:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(scoreboard): render native sidebar title images

Load bounded protocol 2193 sidebar metadata from the accepted converted server resource pack. Match the exact dedicated title font and glyph before replacing the Java sidebar. Render the authored image dimensions and row height while preserving score order, styled entry components and number format. CubeCraft 1.26.51.1 declares a 66 by 21 title image and 10-pixel rows; its 360 by 94 source texture intentionally stretches to that UI size. Reload snapshots reject stale completions and resources from another pack, and disconnect clears prior server state. Tests cover metadata acceptance, identity, dimensions and layout.

Render the declared static sidebar panel background using its original texture, alpha, nine-slice border, content padding and row offsets. Require that the background texture comes from the same accepted server pack as the title metadata. Preserve native corners rather than replacing the frame with two Java rectangles. The saved CubeCraft pack exercises all supported fields; bounded metadata and nine-slice layout tests pass.
